course: dictionary
lesson: 11817
title: Billionaire: a very rich person
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A billionaire is a very rich person. Look inside the word: billion is a huge number, so a billionaire owns money and things worth at least one billion. «Mia's uncle is a tech billionaire who owns a company that makes phones.» The words tech and company are clues that he earned his money from business.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Sara wants to become a billionaire one day.» Replace billionaire with «a very rich person who owns a billion pounds» and the sentence still makes sense. That tells you the meaning fits.
explain: A billion is much bigger than a million. A million has six zeros, and a billion has nine: 1,000,000,000. So a billionaire is far richer than a millionaire, who has at least one million.
fact: A billionaire is a very rich person who owns money and things worth at least one billion dollars, pounds or euros.
fact: One billion is one thousand million: 1,000,000,000.
fact: «A tech billionaire» is a very rich person who made their money from technology companies.
fact: «Become a billionaire» means to grow rich enough to own at least one billion.
fact: Billionaires are often owners of big companies.
exercise: «Her aunt is a billionaire who owns a large company.» What is a billionaire? | A person who counts to one billion | *A very rich person who owns things worth at least one billion | A very kind teacher | A person who works in a bank for one day
exercise: «The news said the tech billionaire gave money to a hospital.» What does tech billionaire mean? | A doctor who works at a hospital | *A very rich person who made money from technology companies | A person who fixes computers for a living | A person who has never had any money
exercise: Which number is one billion? | *1,000,000,000 | 1,000,000 | 1,000 | 100,000,000
test: «Ben said, "When I become a billionaire, I will buy a castle."» What does become a billionaire mean? | *To grow so rich that you own at least one billion | To be born in a big city | To lose all your money | To count to one hundred
test: Which is more money? | Neither, they are both zero | The same amount | *A billion | A million
exam: Which sentence uses billionaire correctly? | Her dog is a billionaire | Billionaire is a colour of paint | *The billionaire bought the big company | We had billionaire for lunch
